[
    {
        "content": "<p>New puzzle for <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110050\">@Sébastien Gouëzel</span> since Brittany is probably the only place in France where thinking is currently possible. Do we have bad diamond here, or is it only the heat wave?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Geometry</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Manifold</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">VectorBundle</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Riemannian</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Geometry</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Manifold</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsManifold</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bundle</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FiniteDimensional</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ModelWithCorners</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">EMetricSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ChartedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">RiemannianBundle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instModuleTangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">instInnerProductSpaceReal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toModule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: Tactic `rfl` failed: The left-hand side</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  instModuleTangentSpace I x</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">is not definitionally equal to the right-hand side</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  (instInnerProductSpaceReal x).toModule</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">E : Type u_1</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">inst✝⁶ : NormedAddCommGroup E</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">inst✝⁵ : NormedSpace ℝ E</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">inst✝⁴ : FiniteDimensional ℝ E</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">H : Type u_2</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">inst✝³ : TopologicalSpace H</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">M : Type u_3</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">inst✝² : EMetricSpace M</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">inst✝¹ : ChartedSpace H M</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">inst✝ : RiemannianBundle fun x =&gt; TangentSpace I x</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">x : M</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">⊢ instModuleTangentSpace I x = (instInnerProductSpaceReal x).toModule</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instModuleTangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">instInnerProductSpaceReal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toModule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">with_reducible</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 606013476,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1782223531
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is currently triggering a <code>set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false</code> need on the Levi-Civita branch.</p>",
        "id": 606013951,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1782223642
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm thinking this could be caused by the right hand side of:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instModuleTangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">instInnerProductSpaceReal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toModule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>?</p>",
        "id": 606014493,
        "sender_full_name": "Amlal El Mahrouss",
        "timestamp": 1782223760
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instModuleTangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">instInnerProductSpaceReal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toModule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">with_reducible_and_instances</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>so does that mean that we don't care that <code>with_reducible rfl</code> fails?</p>",
        "id": 606221322,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1782302346
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, we don't care that <code>with_reducible rfl</code> fails. The important one is <code>with_reducible_and_instances rfl</code>, which succeeds :)</p>",
        "id": 606229561,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1782304552
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don’t understand what “the important one” means. We have a proof at <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36845/changes#diff-1422b931d0bb1bff9b9a8afe7c1414fb3c333d86fcbd410b45f45d3e95093849R280\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36845/changes#diff-1422b931d0bb1bff9b9a8afe7c1414fb3c333d86fcbd410b45f45d3e95093849R280</a> which currently requires <code>set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false</code>. If I squeeze the simp, remove the setting and isolate the failing step I get to</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lcAux₁_apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FiniteDimensional</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">Π</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hX</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MDiffAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">Π</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hY</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MDiffAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">Z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">Π</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hZ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MDiffAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Z</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">⟪</span><span class=\"n\">lcAux₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hY</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">⟫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">leviCivitaAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lcAux₁</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp_rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LinearIsometryEquiv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toContinuousLinearEquiv_symm</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousLinearMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp_apply</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousLinearEquiv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coe_coe</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp_rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LinearIsometryEquiv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coe_symm_toContinuousLinearEquiv</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">InnerProductSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toDual_symm_apply</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">TensorialAt</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mkHom₂_apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hX</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hZ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Where <code>simp only [ContinuousLinearEquiv.coe_coe]</code> makes no progress. Then I turn it into <code>erw? [ContinuousLinearEquiv.coe_coe]</code> which says: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">❌️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">reducible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">transparency</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">instModuleTangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"n\">and</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">toModule</span>\n<span class=\"n\">are</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">defeq</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">but</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">they</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">are</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">transparency</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I understand that <code>simp ≠ rw</code>, but it still seems this transparency issue is somewhat important.</p>",
        "id": 606482233,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1782391825
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I could imagine that <code>erw?</code> is misidentifying the problem</p>",
        "id": 606504736,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1782397072
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>I don’t understand what “the important one” means.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>it's true that there's many \"important one\"s here, so I guess like Jovan said it's the 'erw' tactic that causes the diagnostic? I'm quite recent in Lean so I'm not sure about that one, so if someone has a better diagnostic on this, please let me know</p>",
        "id": 606505995,
        "sender_full_name": "Amlal El Mahrouss",
        "timestamp": 1782397350
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Indeed, it looks like <code>erw?</code> is mistaken. Using <code>#defeq_abuse</code>, I get</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">defeq_abuse</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fails</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">but</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">succeeds</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`false</span><span class=\"bp\">`.</span>\n<span class=\"n\">The</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">following</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isDefEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">checks</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">are</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">root</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">causes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">failure</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">❌️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">starRingEnd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=?=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RingHom</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Indeed,</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">starRingEnd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RingHom</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">with_reducible_and_instances</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>fails.</p>\n<p>Let me try to fix that.</p>",
        "id": 606521255,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1782400773
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41047\">#41047</a></p>",
